-- wra2-s54-esa-commitment.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (UK) ss 54 to 56, employment and support allowance: claimant commitment, work-related activity, hardship payments (interim period).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part wra2. Host Act short name: WRA2007 = Welfare Reform Act 2007; ESA = employment and support allowance.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt (a converter script's plain-text rendering; not the official text).
-- s 54 inserts WRA2007 1(3)(aa), 1C and Schedule 2 para 4A; s 55 inserts 13(8); s 56 inserts 16A.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN where the text points outside the sources (regulations, the Secretary of State's opinion) and BOOLEAN where it closes its own definition.

§ `s 54 Claimant commitment for employment and support allowance`

-- src:925 | (2) In section 1(3) (employment and support allowance: basic conditions) after paragraph (a) there is inserted—
-- src:926 | (aa) has accepted a claimant commitment,
-- src:936 | (6) Regulations may provide that, in prescribed circumstances, a claimant is to be treated as having satisfied the condition mentioned in section 1(3)(aa).
@ref s 54(2) WRA2007 1(3)(aa) with 1C(6) (src:925-926 src:936)
GIVEN `the claimant has accepted a claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations treat the claimant as having satisfied the condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54(2) WRA2007 1(3)(aa) the claimant satisfies the condition of having accepted a claimant commitment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant has accepted a claimant commitment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `regulations treat the claimant as having satisfied the condition`
            -- WRA2007 1C(6): regulations may treat a claimant as having satisfied the condition in prescribed circumstances
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has accepted a claimant commitment" is one of the basic conditions; not accepted, and not treated as satisfied
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the prescribed circumstances are in regulations that are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:941 | 4A
-- src:942 | Regulations may prescribe circumstances in which a person may be entitled to employment and support allowance without having accepted a claimant commitment.
@ref s 54(6) WRA2007 Sch 2 para 4A (src:941-942)
GIVEN `regulations prescribe circumstances in which the person may be entitled without having accepted a claimant commitment, and these are they` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54(6) WRA2007 Sch 2 para 4A the person may be entitled without having accepted a claimant commitment` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Regulations may prescribe circumstances in which a person may be entitled ... without having accepted a claimant commitment"; they are not among the sources
    `regulations prescribe circumstances in which the person may be entitled without having accepted a claimant commitment, and these are they`

§§ `WRA2007 1C: the claimant commitment`

-- src:929 | (1) For the purposes of this Part a “claimant commitment” is a record of the claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of an employment and support allowance.
@ref s 54 WRA2007 1C(1) (src:929)
GIVEN `the award` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54 WRA2007 1C(1) the award is an award of an employment and support allowance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the award`
    WHEN `contributory employment and support allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `income-related employment and support allowance` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to an award of an employment and support allowance" -- an award of any other benefit is not one
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:929 | (1) For the purposes of this Part a “claimant commitment” is a record of the claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of an employment and support allowance.
@ref s 54 WRA2007 1C(1) (src:929)
GIVEN `the document is a record of the claimant's responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the award the record is in relation to` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54 WRA2007 1C(1) the document is a claimant commitment` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “claimant commitment” is a record of the claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of an employment and support allowance" (a definition; "is", not "means", see NOTES)
        `the document is a record of the claimant's responsibilities`
    AND `s 54 WRA2007 1C(1) the award is an award of an employment and support allowance` `the award the record is in relation to`

-- src:930 | (2) A claimant commitment is to be prepared by the Secretary of State and may be reviewed and updated as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
-- src:938 | (5) In section 16(1) (contracting out) before paragraph (a) there is inserted—
-- src:939 | (za) any function under section 1C in relation to a claimant commitment;
@ref s 54 WRA2007 1C(2) with 16(1)(za) (src:930 src:938-939)
GIVEN `who prepared the claimant commitment` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54 WRA2007 1C(2) the claimant commitment was prepared by the Secretary of State` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who prepared the claimant commitment`
    WHEN `the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- s 54(5) inserts 1C functions among those that may be contracted out (WRA2007 16(1)(za))
    WHEN `an authorised person` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is to be prepared by the Secretary of State" says nothing of preparation by anyone else
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:931 | (3) A claimant commitment is to be in such form as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
@ref s 54 WRA2007 1C(3) (src:931)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State thinks the form fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54 WRA2007 1C(3) the claimant commitment is in the form the Secretary of State thinks fit` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant commitment is to be in such form as the Secretary of State thinks fit"
    `the Secretary of State thinks the form fit`

-- src:932 | (4) A claimant commitment is to include—
-- src:933 | (a) any prescribed information, and
-- src:934 | (b) any other information the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include.
@ref s 54 WRA2007 1C(4) (src:932-934)
GIVEN `it includes the prescribed information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it includes any other information the Secretary of State considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54 WRA2007 1C(4) the claimant commitment includes what the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant commitment is to include ... (b) any other information the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include"
        IF NOT `it includes any other information the Secretary of State considers appropriate`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `it includes the prescribed information`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) any prescribed information"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what information is prescribed is left to regulations
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:935 | (5) For the purposes of this Part a claimant accepts a claimant commitment if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it in such manner as may be prescribed.
@ref s 54 WRA2007 1C(5) (src:935)
GIVEN `the claimant accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant accepted it in the manner prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54 WRA2007 1C(5) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "accepts a claimant commitment if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it"
        IF NOT `the claimant accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the claimant accepted it in the manner prescribed`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, and only if, ... accepts ... in such manner as may be prescribed" -- accepted, but not in the prescribed manner
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the manner of acceptance is prescribed in regulations that are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `s 55 Work experience etc`

DECLARE `s 55 WRA2007 13(7) activity` IS ONE OF
    `s 55 WRA2007 13(8) work experience or a work placement`
    `s 55 WRA2007 13(7) some other activity`

-- src:945 | In section 13 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 (work-related activity), after subsection (7) there is inserted—
-- src:946 | (8) The reference to activity in subsection (7) includes work experience or a work placement.
@ref s 55 WRA2007 13(8) (src:945-946)
GIVEN `the activity` IS A `s 55 WRA2007 13(7) activity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55 WRA2007 13(8) the activity is within the reference to activity in subsection (7)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `s 55 WRA2007 13(8) work experience or a work placement` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The reference to activity in subsection (7) includes work experience or a work placement" and does not close the reference
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 56 Hardship payments`

-- src:950 | (1) Regulations may make provision for the making of payments (“hardship payments”) by way of an employment and support allowance to a person where—
-- src:951 | (a) the amount otherwise payable to the person in respect of an employment and support allowance is reduced by virtue of regulations under section 11(3), 12(3) or 13(3), and
-- src:952 | (b) the person is or will be in hardship.
@ref s 56 WRA2007 16A(1) (src:950-952)
GIVEN `the amount otherwise payable is reduced by virtue of regulations under section 11(3), 12(3) or 13(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is or will be in hardship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56 WRA2007 16A(1) regulations may provide for hardship payments to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the amount otherwise payable is reduced by virtue of regulations under section 11(3), 12(3) or 13(3)`
           AND `the person is or will be in hardship`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Regulations may make provision for the making of payments ... where (a) ... and (b) ..." -- the case is outside the power
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2): hardship regulations`

DECLARE `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2)(a) circumstances in which a person is to be treated as being or not being in hardship`
    `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2)(b) matters to be taken into account in determining whether a person is or will be in hardship`
    `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2)(c) requirements or conditions to be met by a person in order to receive hardship payments`
    `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2)(d) the amount or rate of hardship payments`
    `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2)(e) the period for which hardship payments may be made`
    `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2) some other matter`

-- src:953 | (2) Regulations under this section may in particular make provision as to—
-- src:954 | (a) circumstances in which a person is to be treated as being or not being in hardship;
-- src:955 | (b) matters to be taken into account in determining whether a person is or will be in hardship;
-- src:956 | (c) requirements or conditions to be met by a person in order to receive hardship payments;
-- src:957 | (d) the amount or rate of hardship payments;
-- src:958 | (e) the period for which hardship payments may be made.
@ref s 56 WRA2007 16A(2) (src:953-958)
GIVEN `the item` IS A `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56 WRA2007 16A(2) regulations may make provision as to that matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2)(a) circumstances in which a person is to be treated as being or not being in hardship` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2)(b) matters to be taken into account in determining whether a person is or will be in hardship` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2)(c) requirements or conditions to be met by a person in order to receive hardship payments` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2)(d) the amount or rate of hardship payments` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2)(e) the period for which hardship payments may be made` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Regulations under this section may in particular make provision as to" five matters and does not close the list
    WHEN `s 56 WRA2007 16A(2) some other matter` THEN NOTHING

